WEBVTT

00:00:01.420 --> 00:00:05.240
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the Supreme Monarch, Dande...

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:10.240
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew...

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:15.540
This is the story of
their lives and adventures.

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:27.460
Here goes! Go!

00:00:29.030 --> 00:00:30.260
Come at me, Satoshi!

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:40.400
It’s over!

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:42.650
That was nothing...!

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:54.630
Okay! No, it’s not...

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:57.320
I’ve gotta get way, way stronger...

00:00:57.320 --> 00:00:59.870
...if I wanna keep up with
Kamonegi’s training.

00:00:59.870 --> 00:01:01.420
Owww...

00:01:01.420 --> 00:01:05.310
Still, is there any point in
practicing fencing with leeks?

00:01:05.310 --> 00:01:06.640
Sure there is!

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:08.520
Aim to be a Leek Master!

00:01:17.070 --> 00:01:18.340
That’s a huge rock you smashed...!

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:19.690
You’re amazing, Kamonegi!

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:23.850
It’s getting better and better
at handling its leek!

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:24.520
Yeah.

00:01:25.190 --> 00:01:29.090
Ever since it lost to Earlade,
it’s been training everyday.

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:34.120
So I want to help it train...
as much as I can!

00:01:34.120 --> 00:01:36.140
Hey! Satoshi!

00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:37.550
Oh, Director!

00:01:37.550 --> 00:01:40.960
You were looking for a place
where Kamonegi can train, weren’t you?

00:01:42.850 --> 00:01:45.250
Renji found something interesting.

00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:47.770
Did you find somewhere good?

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:50.420
This is over in the Kalos region, but...

00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:52.320
“The Castle of Chivalry.”

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:56.430
“Pokémon and trainers
seeking true strength are welcome!”

00:01:56.430 --> 00:02:01.220
“Hot-blooded coaching by Gampi
of the Kalos Elite Four”... Wow!

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:05.430
The Elite Four are the strongest trainers
of a given region, right?

00:02:05.430 --> 00:02:06.440
Yeah!

00:02:07.450 --> 00:02:09.900
Kamonegi, should we try it?

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:12.820
Yeah!

00:02:14.790 --> 00:02:16.450
Oh, Strike!

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:21.680
Do you want to go too, Strike?

00:02:22.710 --> 00:02:27.260
I get it. I haven’t taken you out
to battle much lately...

00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:29.080
Okay! Come with us!

00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:33.590
All right! Let’s go to Kalos!

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:39.850
Trying to become stronger,
Satoshi and Go departed for Kalos.

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:44.630
What awaits them in the
Castle of Chivalry?

00:04:22.450 --> 00:04:23.660
The Castle of Chivalry, Kalos Region

00:04:23.660 --> 00:04:25.330
So this is the Castle of Chivalry...
It certainly looks the part!
The Castle of Chivalry, Kalos Region

00:04:25.330 --> 00:04:27.400
So this is the Castle of Chivalry...
It certainly looks the part!

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:29.660
How are we supposed to get in?

00:04:35.190 --> 00:04:38.850
Thou who seekest strength,
I welcome thee here!

00:04:38.850 --> 00:04:43.550
I am the Man of Steel
of the Kalos Elite Four, Gampi!

00:04:43.550 --> 00:04:45.560
He’s really intense...

00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:49.860
I believe chivalry to be
the path of the truly strong.

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:55.530
And in order to convey such to
trainers and Pokémon around the world,

00:04:55.530 --> 00:04:58.030
I established this Castle of Chivalry!

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:06.060
Gilgard! Royal Sword Pokémon!
Steel/Ghost type!

00:05:06.060 --> 00:05:10.360
It fights by switching between
two Formes: attack and defense!

00:05:10.360 --> 00:05:14.290
It can use spectral power
to control people and Pokémon!

00:05:14.290 --> 00:05:18.140
Now! Let us seek
new heights together!

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:20.300
Yeah.

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:21.800
Thank you!

00:05:23.180 --> 00:05:24.430
Good answers!

00:05:24.430 --> 00:05:27.180
Oh, how refreshing thy bright eyes are!

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:30.430
Glory be to thy futures!

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:32.580
H-He’s crying?

00:05:32.580 --> 00:05:34.800
He seems really passionate...

00:05:37.340 --> 00:05:39.070
Challengers,
I ask for your names!

00:05:39.070 --> 00:05:42.320
I’m Satoshi!
This is my partner, Pikachu.

00:05:43.580 --> 00:05:46.180
We came here to train Kamonegi.

00:05:46.830 --> 00:05:49.700
I’m Go! And this is Strike!

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:52.170
My, what wonderful expressions.

00:05:54.250 --> 00:05:56.170
This one shall be a worthy student!

00:06:00.580 --> 00:06:02.750
Oh, this is so cool!

00:06:02.750 --> 00:06:06.970
Yeah. But why do <i>we</i>
have to wear armor, too?

00:06:06.970 --> 00:06:11.070
There is but one reason!
Since ye dost pursue true strength!

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:14.600
Ye shall discover why
as soon as your training begins!

00:06:14.600 --> 00:06:18.110
We will?
I’m getting excited!

00:06:18.110 --> 00:06:22.690
This Castle of Chivalry is composed of
three different training grounds.

00:06:23.170 --> 00:06:29.480
When Pokémon and trainer overcome
the three tasks together, and reach the roof...

00:06:29.480 --> 00:06:35.120
As proof of their true strength, they shall be bestowed
Knight Medals to honor their title as knights!

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:36.600
Knight Medals...

00:06:36.600 --> 00:06:38.670
We’ll get ‘em for sure,
Kamonegi!

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:43.270
We begin with the first task!

00:06:43.270 --> 00:06:45.590
A knight must show
peerless strength!

00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:48.390
One must polish and hone oneself!

00:06:48.390 --> 00:06:50.380
Showing peerless strength...

00:06:50.380 --> 00:06:52.930
Then we’re starting
with battle training?!

00:06:53.890 --> 00:06:57.460
Run ten laps around the castle!

00:06:57.460 --> 00:06:58.650
What?!

00:07:00.360 --> 00:07:03.240
Yeah! Thanks for
cheering me on, Pikachu!

00:07:04.360 --> 00:07:07.940
So we’re building stamina!
Well, that’s the place to start!

00:07:07.940 --> 00:07:11.540
Ten laps isn’t exactly easy, though.

00:07:11.540 --> 00:07:13.120
This armor’s pretty heavy, too.

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:14.850
It’s no big deal!

00:07:14.850 --> 00:07:18.250
We’ve gotta be able to do this, no sweat!
Right, Kamonegi?

00:07:20.370 --> 00:07:23.170
Kamonegi and Strike are both
super determined, huh?

00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:26.430
Wh-What’s that?

00:07:27.590 --> 00:07:31.520
Dainose! Compass Pokémon!
Rock/Steel type!

00:07:31.520 --> 00:07:33.790
It exudes strong magnetism
from all over!

00:07:33.790 --> 00:07:38.770
It freely controls three units
called Mini-Noses!

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:42.230
Dainose, huh?
I wonder what it’s doing here.

00:07:42.230 --> 00:07:44.740
It must’ve come here
to train too, right?

00:07:48.700 --> 00:07:50.120
Wh-What?!

00:07:50.120 --> 00:07:52.240
My body’s suddenly so heavy...

00:07:52.750 --> 00:07:56.630
Dainose is my companion,
aiding in the first task!

00:07:56.630 --> 00:08:02.570
Withstanding and outrunning its strong magnetic field
builds a strong mind and a strong body!

00:08:04.390 --> 00:08:05.780
So that was it!

00:08:05.780 --> 00:08:08.470
But... This is pretty tough,
you know?!

00:08:11.680 --> 00:08:13.450
Kamonegi!

00:08:18.030 --> 00:08:19.600
And Strike!

00:08:19.600 --> 00:08:21.610
All right! We aren’t gonna...

00:08:21.610 --> 00:08:23.450
...give up either, yeah?!

00:08:26.120 --> 00:08:29.860
Yes! Your steadfast hearts pushing onward
are marvelous!

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:34.200
It stopped!

00:08:42.440 --> 00:08:46.860
Good work running!
Ye have all passed the first task!

00:08:46.860 --> 00:08:48.810
We did it...

00:08:49.870 --> 00:08:54.220
My joints are creaking,
but that felt good!

00:08:56.220 --> 00:09:00.900
What extraordinary resolve
I have witnessed from you!

00:09:03.160 --> 00:09:06.110
Keep that fighting spirit
and proceed!

00:09:06.110 --> 00:09:08.920
Now, to the second task!

00:09:11.090 --> 00:09:14.830
This is the site of the second task,
the Maze of Doubts!

00:09:16.820 --> 00:09:18.800
The Maze of Doubts?

00:09:18.800 --> 00:09:21.250
It looks like a creepy place.

00:09:22.400 --> 00:09:24.460
A knight must show
peerless bravery!

00:09:25.630 --> 00:09:29.380
Fears and doubts constantly
assail one on the battlefield.

00:09:29.870 --> 00:09:36.390
Pokémon and trainer must work hand in hand
to escape this maze filled with traps!

00:09:36.390 --> 00:09:40.490
I see... Let’s do our best
to get through, Strike!

00:09:41.850 --> 00:09:45.210
We aren’t giving up either!
Right, Kamonegi?

00:09:45.210 --> 00:09:48.650
Huh? Hey, wait for me!
Let’s go together!

00:09:49.070 --> 00:09:51.330
No change with Kamonegi, I see.

00:09:51.900 --> 00:09:53.210
Hold on!

00:09:54.990 --> 00:09:59.770
This task tests the bond between
the pair of Pokémon and trainer.

00:09:59.770 --> 00:10:03.790
Thou mayest wait for everyone
at the exit, alongside me.

00:10:04.450 --> 00:10:06.380
Pikachu, I’ll see you later!

00:10:17.280 --> 00:10:19.010
The path splits in two...

00:10:19.010 --> 00:10:23.680
We’ve reached the crossroads of destiny...
Which way should we go?

00:10:24.530 --> 00:10:25.530
What’s that?

00:10:27.190 --> 00:10:29.050
The die has been cast!

00:10:29.050 --> 00:10:30.740
Looks like it.

00:10:30.740 --> 00:10:32.550
Let’s meet up at the goal, Go!

00:10:32.550 --> 00:10:33.580
Yeah!

00:10:37.910 --> 00:10:39.630
What?

00:10:54.930 --> 00:10:56.430
That was great, Strike!

00:10:57.890 --> 00:10:59.980
Okay, let’s keep going!

00:11:09.590 --> 00:11:11.410
The path splits again...

00:11:12.070 --> 00:11:12.990
Hey, Kamonegi!

00:11:14.950 --> 00:11:17.050
Ah, Dedenne!

00:11:18.040 --> 00:11:19.900
Why’s a Dedenne here?

00:11:20.700 --> 00:11:22.340
That tickles!

00:11:29.210 --> 00:11:31.460
Hey! Wait for me!

00:11:39.660 --> 00:11:41.810
Kamonegi! Look out!

00:11:48.650 --> 00:11:51.730
Huh? A dead end?

00:11:51.730 --> 00:11:54.990
Oh, well... Let’s go back
and take the other path.

00:11:56.110 --> 00:11:56.900
Kamonegi?

00:11:59.830 --> 00:12:01.530
What? Really?

00:12:13.630 --> 00:12:16.110
Wow...

00:12:16.110 --> 00:12:18.590
What? What’s going on now?

00:12:18.590 --> 00:12:23.100
That Kamonegi has rare gifts
in fighting spirit and power.

00:12:23.650 --> 00:12:29.120
A lone warrior who follows its own path
and never backs down.

00:12:29.120 --> 00:12:31.160
What wonderful talent.

00:12:31.160 --> 00:12:32.110
However...

00:12:32.590 --> 00:12:36.610
As it is, it cannot hope to
achieve true strength!

00:12:38.450 --> 00:12:40.490
I wonder how much longer
until we reach the goal...

00:12:45.040 --> 00:12:45.950
Kamonegi!

00:12:50.640 --> 00:12:52.630
Kamonegi! I’ll save you!

00:12:59.630 --> 00:13:00.580
Nearly there...!

00:13:05.020 --> 00:13:06.020
Your leek!

00:13:15.560 --> 00:13:17.490
Pocket Monsters!

00:13:43.440 --> 00:13:45.110
That was close.

00:13:45.710 --> 00:13:47.890
Here. I’m glad it’s safe.

00:13:49.970 --> 00:13:52.560
That leek is what’s most
important to you, after all!

00:13:54.610 --> 00:13:56.570
Now, let’s hurry on ahead!

00:14:00.440 --> 00:14:03.950
Hmm? A sign of change, perhaps?

00:14:09.950 --> 00:14:10.890
Satoshi.

00:14:10.890 --> 00:14:13.470
Go? That means...

00:14:13.470 --> 00:14:14.460
The goal?

00:14:15.990 --> 00:14:18.460
Yes! Ye have passed
the second task!

00:14:18.460 --> 00:14:19.690
We did it!

00:14:19.690 --> 00:14:21.330
We passed!

00:14:24.930 --> 00:14:28.380
Marvelous, truly marvelous!

00:14:30.870 --> 00:14:34.480
Let me express my sincere respect
for making it this far.

00:14:37.790 --> 00:14:42.710
Now, this is the last: the third task.
Take care as ye proceed.

00:14:48.990 --> 00:14:51.060
This looks pretty barren...

00:14:51.060 --> 00:14:52.770
I wonder what the task is?

00:14:52.770 --> 00:14:55.810
Now, ye shall undergo
the third task.

00:14:56.500 --> 00:15:01.710
As I stated beforehand, those who pass this
will be awarded Knight Medals.

00:15:01.710 --> 00:15:03.970
Your task is simple and clear.

00:15:04.480 --> 00:15:09.470
Open the locked door behind me,
and ye wilt have passed.

00:15:10.160 --> 00:15:13.110
And as for the key to the door...

00:15:16.090 --> 00:15:16.850
Cleffy!

00:15:17.750 --> 00:15:22.250
Cleffy! Key Ring Pokémon!
Steel/Fairy type!

00:15:22.250 --> 00:15:25.010
It absorbs metal ions
through its horn!

00:15:25.010 --> 00:15:27.740
It has a habit of collecting keys!

00:15:27.740 --> 00:15:33.920
If trainer and Pokémon work together
to take the key from this Cleffy, and open the door,

00:15:33.920 --> 00:15:35.460
ye shall all pass.

00:15:36.030 --> 00:15:37.000
However...

00:15:37.640 --> 00:15:39.420
Taking it will not be easy!

00:15:41.460 --> 00:15:43.420
So that’s it.

00:15:46.910 --> 00:15:48.290
Are ye prepared?

00:15:50.020 --> 00:15:53.350
Now! Now!
To battle! To battle! To battle!

00:15:53.350 --> 00:15:55.980
We just need to take that key, right?

00:15:55.980 --> 00:15:58.850
He who strikes first wins!
Kamonegi! Crossroad Kill!

00:15:59.690 --> 00:16:01.230
Strike, use Slash!

00:16:02.650 --> 00:16:04.030
Guard, Gilgard!

00:16:10.370 --> 00:16:11.490
Consecutive Cut!

00:16:11.490 --> 00:16:12.450
Air Slash!

00:16:20.670 --> 00:16:22.510
That Gilgard’s really tough...

00:16:23.020 --> 00:16:23.750
Hold on...

00:16:23.750 --> 00:16:27.510
He never said <i>we</i> couldn’t
take the key, did he?

00:16:27.510 --> 00:16:30.510
Oh, right!
Then while we have the chance...!

00:16:30.510 --> 00:16:32.390
The key’s ours!

00:16:32.390 --> 00:16:35.140
I believe I said taking it
would not be easy!

00:16:36.650 --> 00:16:38.480
You’re fighting too,
Mr. Gampi?

00:16:39.430 --> 00:16:42.350
These are replica swords
for the training here,

00:16:42.350 --> 00:16:45.010
but they are still
not to be taken lightly.

00:16:45.010 --> 00:16:46.860
Now, to battle!

00:16:47.220 --> 00:16:49.780
So this is why you had us
wear the armor?

00:16:50.880 --> 00:16:54.240
See, Go? Fencing with leeks
really did help!

00:17:11.900 --> 00:17:13.630
What’s the matter?
Is that all ye have?

00:17:14.970 --> 00:17:16.480
We’re not getting anywhere like this.

00:17:16.480 --> 00:17:18.730
Okay, I’ll stall Mr. Gampi.

00:17:18.730 --> 00:17:19.280
Huh?!

00:17:19.280 --> 00:17:21.910
Kamonegi, can you
take care of Gilgard?

00:17:22.750 --> 00:17:26.360
Go and Strike, you take the key from Cleffy
while they’re busy!

00:17:26.360 --> 00:17:27.280
Got it.

00:17:29.430 --> 00:17:30.440
Let’s go!

00:17:32.430 --> 00:17:34.120
Hold on!

00:17:34.620 --> 00:17:36.690
A brave decision.

00:17:36.690 --> 00:17:39.790
But also reckless,
wouldn’t thou agree?

00:17:39.790 --> 00:17:41.110
I’m not giving up!

00:17:41.110 --> 00:17:43.250
Hmm? Then thou shalt
have to do better!

00:17:51.220 --> 00:17:53.140
Gilgard! King’s Shield!

00:18:07.530 --> 00:18:10.740
It’s just like with Earlade.
That approach won’t work!

00:18:10.740 --> 00:18:13.070
Dost thou have the liberty
to be looking away?!

00:18:16.760 --> 00:18:20.490
Stop!

00:18:23.460 --> 00:18:24.770
Strike!

00:18:31.280 --> 00:18:34.180
You don’t have to thank me.
We’re both helping each other!

00:18:35.260 --> 00:18:38.720
Let’s give it one more go!
Corner it from either side!

00:18:39.790 --> 00:18:40.310
Go!

00:18:44.060 --> 00:18:45.530
This is the end!

00:18:51.100 --> 00:18:52.730
I’m glad it’s safe.

00:18:54.310 --> 00:18:57.290
That leek is what’s most
important to you, after all!

00:18:59.490 --> 00:19:01.660
Gilgard! Sacred Sword!

00:19:05.120 --> 00:19:08.230
Thy Kamonegi cannot
defeat Gilgard!

00:19:08.980 --> 00:19:10.690
No way it can’t!

00:19:10.690 --> 00:19:12.260
I believe in Kamonegi!

00:19:13.330 --> 00:19:14.840
Then you shall believe...

00:19:19.930 --> 00:19:21.850
...as you are struck down together!

00:19:24.890 --> 00:19:26.810
Kamonegi, you...

00:19:29.130 --> 00:19:32.200
It rushed to its trainer,
despite having to take damage...

00:19:34.700 --> 00:19:37.790
But it cannot withstand
another attack!

00:19:37.790 --> 00:19:39.740
Gilgard! Sacred Sword!

00:19:45.830 --> 00:19:47.330
That’s... Detect!

00:19:48.460 --> 00:19:50.500
Okay! Keep going
and use Crossroad Kill!

00:19:56.970 --> 00:19:57.880
Hold on, Kamonegi!

00:20:01.720 --> 00:20:04.060
We got the key!

00:20:04.410 --> 00:20:05.680
Marvelous!

00:20:07.290 --> 00:20:14.150
A knight is one who fights to protect their precious lord,
and the weak and powerless.

00:20:14.150 --> 00:20:20.870
When one truly treasures another, and fights to protect them,
their strength is magnified manyfold.

00:20:20.990 --> 00:20:25.500
Sir Satoshi, Sir Kamonegi,
Sir Go, Sir Strike...

00:20:25.500 --> 00:20:31.840
I hereby acknowledge your success in training,
and award you these Knight Medals!

00:20:32.810 --> 00:20:34.340
The Knight Medals...

00:20:34.340 --> 00:20:35.840
...are ours!

00:20:37.750 --> 00:20:43.330
By the way, Sir Go, hast thou ever considered
evolving thy partner, Sir Strike?

00:20:46.670 --> 00:20:51.740
If thou transferrest Strike as it holds
this item, a Metal Coat...

00:20:57.980 --> 00:21:01.070
Whoa! It evolved into Hassam!

00:21:02.150 --> 00:21:03.810
I’m happy for you, Hassam!

00:21:06.280 --> 00:21:09.750
Hassam’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:21:09.750 --> 00:21:13.950
Hassam! Pincer Pokémon!
Bug/Steel type!

00:21:13.950 --> 00:21:18.260
It smashes enemies
with pincers hard as steel!

00:21:18.940 --> 00:21:21.980
Mr. Gampi,
thank you so much for today!

00:21:21.980 --> 00:21:24.670
Indeed!
Be sure to keep training diligently!

00:21:24.670 --> 00:21:25.600
Right!

00:21:25.600 --> 00:21:30.060
Kamonegi! Let’s beat Earlade
next time, you hear?

00:21:32.040 --> 00:21:38.670
Satoshi and Kamonegi, and Go and Hassam have learned
the way of the knight; strong, brave, and kind.

00:21:39.180 --> 00:21:43.040
Their days of dreams, adventures and
training are sure to continue!

00:21:50.870 --> 00:21:51.540
Pikachu!

00:21:51.540 --> 00:21:52.410
Utsubot!

00:21:52.410 --> 00:21:53.120
Transel!

00:21:53.120 --> 00:21:53.920
Lugia!

00:21:53.920 --> 00:21:54.710
Achamo!

00:21:54.710 --> 00:21:55.500
Morpeko!

00:21:55.500 --> 00:21:56.210
Koduck!

00:21:56.210 --> 00:21:57.090
Cleffy!

00:21:57.090 --> 00:21:57.790
Eevee!

00:21:57.790 --> 00:21:58.540
Ishitsubute!

00:21:58.540 --> 00:21:59.210
Teppouo!

00:21:59.210 --> 00:22:00.130
Onisuzume!

00:22:00.130 --> 00:22:00.840
